 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nPRQL aggregate function parsing broken after recent changes\n\n#### Description\n\nThe PRQL dialect's `_parse_aggregate` method is failing to parse aggregate functions correctly. When trying to parse PRQL queries with aggregate functions, the parser throws an `UnboundLocalError` for the variable `name`.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport sqlglot\n\n# This should work but currently fails\nquery = \"from a aggregate { average x }\"\nresult = sqlglot.transpile(query, read=\"prql\", write=\"\")\n```\n\nThe error occurs when parsing any PRQL query containing aggregate functions like `average`, `min`, `max`, `sum`, etc.\n\n#### Expected Behavior\n\nThe query should successfully parse and transpile to SQL:\n```sql\nSELECT AVG(x) FROM a\n```\n\n#### Actual Behavior\n\nThe parser raises an `UnboundLocalError: local variable 'name' referenced before assignment` when trying to process the aggregate function.\n\nThis affects all PRQL queries that use aggregate functions, making the PRQL dialect essentially unusable for aggregation operations.\n</issue>\n",
